Feature: Tasks API Integration

  @allure.label.suite:Tasks
  @allure.label.tag:api
  @allure.label.tag:integration
  Scenario: User creates task and can retrieve it
    Given the user is authenticated in a project
    When the user creates a task via API
    Then the task creation should return status 200
    And the task should have a valid ID
    When the user retrieves tasks in the project
    Then the newly created task should be in the list

  @allure.label.suite:Tasks
  @allure.label.tag:api
  @allure.label.tag:integration
  Scenario: User can assign task to team member
    Given the user is authenticated in a team with members
    And a task exists
    When the user assigns the task to a team member
    Then the assignment should return status 200
    When the assignee retrieves their tasks
    Then the newly assigned task should appear in their list

  @allure.label.suite:Tasks
  @allure.label.tag:api
  @allure.label.tag:integration
  Scenario: Task status transitions flow through multiple states
    Given a task exists in "To Do" status
    When the task is updated to "In Progress"
    Then the API should return status 200
    When the task is updated to "In Review"
    Then the API should return status 200
    When the task is updated to "Complete"
    Then the status should be persisted
    When the user retrieves the task
    Then the status should be "Complete"

  @allure.label.suite:Tasks
  @allure.label.tag:api
  @allure.label.tag:integration
  Scenario: Multiple users can sequentially update task state
    Given user A and user B are in the same team
    When user A creates a task
    And user B retrieves the newly created task
    Then user B should see the task
    When user B assigns the task to themselves
    And user A updates the task description
    Then both operations should succeed with status 200

  @allure.label.suite:Tasks
  @allure.label.tag:api
  @allure.label.tag:integration
  Scenario: Task deletion removes it from all queries
    Given a task exists in a project
    When the user deletes the task
    Then the deletion should return status 200
    When the user retrieves project tasks
    Then the deleted task should not be in the list
    When the user attempts to retrieve the deleted task directly
    Then the API should return status 404

  @allure.label.suite:Tasks
  @allure.label.tag:api
  @allure.label.tag:integration
  Scenario: Users can only see tasks assigned to them or created by them
    Given user A and user B in the same team
    When user A creates a task and does not assign it
    And user B retrieves their task list
    Then user B should not see user A's unassigned task
    When user A assigns the task to user B
    And user B retrieves their task list again
    Then the task should now appear in user B's list
